The rest of the chain checks out, so I have enough to answer. The single root cause is the wire delay on the travel-plan → seat connection. Its effect reaches ts-ui-dashboard through travel-plan's travel-plan endpoints. Restarts are flat, and the other tail shifts are small samples with stable medians.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-travel-plan-service",
      "fault_kind": "network_delay",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.service_name AS caller, s.service_name AS callee, COUNT(*) n, ROUND(quantile_cont(c.duration,0.5)/1e6,1) cli_p50_ms, ROUND(quantile_cont(s.duration,0.5)/1e6,1) srv_p50_ms, ROUND(quantile_cont(c.duration,0.5)/1e6 - quantile_cont(s.duration,0.5)/1e6,1) gap_p50_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON s.parent_span_id=c.span_id AND s.attr_span_kind='Server' WHERE c.service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' AND s.service_name='ts-seat-service' GROUP BY 1,2",
          "claim": "Travel-plan to seat left_tickets calls take ~2454 ms at client but ~14 ms in seat's server span, a ~2.4 s gap on the wire."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT 'norm' p, COUNT(*) n, ROUND(quantile_cont(c.duration,0.5)/1e6,1) cli_p50_ms, ROUND(quantile_cont(s.duration,0.5)/1e6,1) srv_p50_ms FROM normal_traces c JOIN normal_traces s ON s.parent_span_id=c.span_id AND s.attr_span_kind='Server' WHERE c.service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' AND s.service_name='ts-seat-service'",
          "claim": "In the normal period the same travel-plan to seat calls had client and server medians of about 13 ms, so there was no gap."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT metric, attr_source, attr_destination, COUNT(*) n, ROUND(AVG(value),1) avg_val FROM abnormal_metrics_sum WHERE metric IN ('hubble_flows_processed_total','hubble_tcp_flags_total','hubble_drop_total') AND attr_source LIKE '%ts-travel-plan%' AND attr_destination LIKE '%ts-seat%' GROUP BY 1,2,3",
          "claim": "Hubble flows and TCP flag counters on the travel-plan to seat connection are elevated in the abnormal period, with no drops recorded."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "ts-travel-plan-service",
      "to": "ts-ui-dashboard",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, COUNT(*) n, ROUND(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,1) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name IN ('ts-ui-dashboard','ts-travel-plan-service') AND attr_span_kind='Server' AND span_name LIKE '%travelPlan%' GROUP BY 1,2 ORDER BY p95_ms DESC",
          "claim": "User-facing travelPlan requests at ts-ui-dashboard take 18–20 s at p95, matching travel-plan's server spans, versus under 1 s before."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

